❮ Scanner Methods

Thelocale()method returns aLocaleobject describing the locale used when interpreting numbers. The locale specifies formatting such as which character is used as a decimal point and how digits in large numbers are grouped.

❮ Scanner Methods

### Code Snippets

```
Example
Show the locale that is currently being used by the scanner:
// Create a scanner object
Scanner myObj = new Scanner("A string to scan");

// Find the locale
System.out.println(myObj.locale());
```
